DECIDE SEMANTICS BEFORE ENCODING
1. Identify what EACH document actually represents. Independently cite anchor_a_ids
   and anchor_b_ids. Shared site chrome, company ownership, a brand, a menu, a
   category link or legal text cannot bind a particular attached product or list.
2. Review EVERY unique span of both sides, reconstructing its local meaning with
   shared context. Lexical uniqueness is not a retained semantic difference.
3. a_meaning_in_b asks whether B preserves ALL meaning in A; b_meaning_in_a asks
   whether A preserves ALL meaning in B. These are not replacement direction names.
4. For each UNCOVERED side select ONE decisive own unique source_span_id and
   explain the lost proposition. Select one closest opposite/shared counterpart_span_id
   if it really exists. Discuss other losses in coverage_explanation; do not hide
   two-sided losses behind a witness on only one side.

NONEMPTY RECORD ANCHORS
SAME_SUBSTANTIVE_RECORD requires both sides independently to represent the same
specific retained record. Ask what B still says about the specific subject after
shared navigation/footer is set aside. If nothing, it is not a record core in B.
A product tag page with actual listings against only the same store navigation is
DISTINCT_OR_UNBOUND_RECORDS, not same-record extension. A shared list of category
links is not an actual matching result list. Same company ownership does not bind
an attached biography, product, event, job or essay.
Two independently identified copies of the same FAQ, recruitment record, product
or organization description may have one-sided factual/procedural extensions.
Missing fields can be additions; conflicting retained values are not additions.
Give the strongest specific conflict type before ordinary extra facts.

NON-MAIN MESSAGES ARE NOT AUTOMATICALLY EQUIVALENT
NON_MAIN_MESSAGES covers cookie/legal/auth/error/navigation/platform messages.
Their purpose, permission, target, controller, scope, state and explanations matter.
An added obligation, access requirement, data-use purpose, withdrawal consequence,
definition or troubleshooting instruction can be UNCOVERED without contradiction.
Consistency, shortness, standard wording or absence of conflict is NOT coverage.
Names matter only in their actually evidenced role; do not invent users, sessions,
record identities or effective dates from headings, buttons or isolated dates.

PAIRED BOUNDARIES
- Same notice plus Accept/Settings/Payment buttons: harmless controls. Same notice
  plus a new access condition, permission or factual consequence: retained loss.
- A complete same-meaning translation: bilateral coverage. Reconstruct translated
  clauses with shared fragments; do not call each alignment fragment a new rule.
  Changed permissions/actions/values are not language differences.
- Repeating exactly the same paragraph twice adds no fact. A soft hyphen adds no
  meaning. Both can be COVERED, but neither implies byte-identical source text.
  A new procedure or changed number alongside repetition is still retained.
- Same FAQ plus a new reset step, or same recruitment record plus an application
  method: one-sided MAIN_CONTENT loss. Do not infer an unstated method from the
  topic, usual practice, or a spam-protection placeholder alone.
- General site prose plus a short author/Stories link can be navigation. Actual
  biography facts, independent members or a separately targeted page are retained.
- Generic tax/shipping/quantity-validation messages do not establish an actual
  order or failure. Explicit state/price/eligibility for an identified record does.

SCOPE AND LOSS TYPES
Use SAME_SUBSTANTIVE_RECORD, NON_MAIN_MESSAGES, DISTINCT_OR_UNBOUND_RECORDS or
UNRESOLVED as warranted. Byte-exact identity is owned by the pre-request router
and is not an option in this critic. Never force a nonexact pair into a same-record
scope simply because it shares words. Insufficient evidence stays UNRESOLVED.
MAIN_CONTENT is a same-record fact or procedure. POLICY_MEANING is retained
non-main permission/purpose/definition/obligation; RECORD_IDENTITY is the actual
subject/recipient/service/controller; PAGE_ROLE is evidenced page function;
STATE_VERSION is a factual state/version; MEMBERSHIP is actual retained members.
OTHER_RETAINED is for a genuine loss not fitting a more specific type.

STATUS/MODE AND SELECTION
- UNCOVERED always uses NOT_COVERED, a non-NONE uncovered_type, a nonempty
  source_span_id, retention_consequence and NO_EQUIVALENT_FOUND or CONTRADICTS.
  Partial overlap is not MIXED. CONTRADICTS requires an actual contrary counterpart.
- COVERED + SEMANTIC_COUNTERPARTS or MIXED requires independent opposite/shared
  coverage_counterpart_ids and a matching proposition, not merely the same topic.
  MIXED means ALL meanings covered through counterparts plus harmless controls.
- COVERED + HARMLESS_ONLY or NO_UNIQUE_SPANS has empty coverage_counterpart_ids.
  Use NO_UNIQUE_SPANS only when that side has no unique spans; repetition is harmless.
- UNRESOLVED uses NOT_COVERED with empty coverage_counterpart_ids.
- COVERED/UNRESOLVED require uncovered_type NONE, empty source_span_id,
  counterpart_span_id and retention_consequence, and counterpart_relation NOT_APPLICABLE.
- Incomplete review uses input_status UNRESOLVED, record_scope UNRESOLVED, empty
  anchors and both side statuses UNRESOLVED. Do not guess a negative.

IDs in reviewed_unique_ids may be explicit lists or ranges, e.g. A001-A004,A006;
they must include all own unique spans for a resolved side, never S IDs.
Anchors and coverage_counterpart_ids may likewise be lists/ranges on the correct side.
source_span_id and counterpart_span_id are different: each is ONE ID or an empty
string, never a range, list, quoted text or invented ID. Source must be own unique;
counterpart must be opposite or shared. The program extracts the full selected span
verbatim. Selection proves source location, not semantic entailment: explain why
the actual opposite meaning fails to preserve the retained proposition.

Keep each explanation to one or two concise factual sentences. Do not put a long
internal debate in the response. Never change a genuine loss into coverage just
to avoid evidence. Return every required field, including inactive empty strings.
